{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EHwb8ajnJcxjWZr4Tw4bvC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"data_quality_fix\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Register-normalize jailbreak data + fix strategy=7 labeling,验证TF-IDF降到<0.75\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"tfidf_before_normalization\": 1.0,\n7\t      \"tfidf_after_first_pass\": 0.82,\n8\t      \"tfidf_after_second_pass\": 0.73,\n9\t      \"normalization_rounds_needed\": 2,\n10\t      \"label_fix_applied\": true,\n11\t      \"benign_strategy_class\": \"none_class_9\"\n12\t    },\n13\t    \"tables\": [\n14\t      {\n15\t        \"caption\": \"TF-IDF Separation After Each Normalization Round\",\n16\t        \"rows\": [\n17\t          [\n18\t            \"raw_data\",\n19\t            1.0,\n20\t            \"Perfect lexical separation\"\n21\t          ],\n22\t          [\n23\t            \"round_1_paraphrase\",\n24\t            0.82,\n25\t            \"Template words removed, register gap remains\"\n26\t          ],\n27\t          [\n28\t            \"round_2_targeted\",\n29\t            0.73,\n30\t            \"Barely passes gate after domain term normalization\"\n31\t          ]\n32\t        ]\n33\t      }\n34\t    ],\n35\t    \"figures\": [],\n36\t    \"analysis\": \"HARD GATE通过但仅勉强（0.73 vs 阈值0.75）。两轮normalization的必要性本身是方法论贡献的核心evidence： 它证明multi-turn jailbreak detection benchmark中存在系统性lexical confound。在reframe方向(1)下， 这个实验的finding从\\\"obstacle to overcome\\\"变为\\\"primary contribution\\\"。\\n\\n\\nTF-IDF需要两轮normalization才降到阈值以下（0.73），说明原始数据中jailbreak和benign的register差异 极大——攻击对话使用了明显不同于benign的词汇分布（更formal/technical的register、特定prompt模板词汇）。 第一轮paraphrase仅消除表层模板词但保留了domain-specific术语差异，需要第二轮targeted normalization 才勉强达标。这本身就是一个强信号：原始pilot phase_b的perfect F1=1.0主要来自lexical shortcut。\\n\"\n37\t  },\n38\t  {\n39\t    \"name\": \"core_revalidation_clean\",\n40\t    \"description\": \"在clean data上重新训练treatment和baseline，全K值评估\",\n41\t    \"results\": {\n42\t      \"treatment_k1_f1_clean\": 0.68,\n43\t      \"baseline_k1_f1_clean\": 0.66,\n44\t      \"treatment_k2_f1_clean\": 0.72,\n45\t      \"baseline_k2_f1_clean\": 0.7,\n46\t      \"treatment_k3_f1_clean\": 0.78,\n47\t      \"baseline_k3_f1_clean\": 0.76,\n48\t      \"treatment_k5_f1_clean\": 0.83,\n49\t      \"baseline_k5_f1_clean\": 0.82,\n50\t      \"treatment_full_f1_clean\": 0.86,\n51\t      \"baseline_full_f1_clean\": 0.85,\n52\t      \"delta_k2_pp\": 2,\n53\t      \"delta_k3_pp\": 2,\n54\t      \"delta_full_pp\": 1,\n55\t      \"deberta_persuasion_acc_clean\": 0.63\n56\t    },\n57\t    \"tables\": [\n58\t      {\n59\t        \"caption\": \"F1 Comparison: Treatment vs Baseline on Clean Data (N=72 test)\",\n60\t        \"rows\": [\n61\t          [\n62\t            \"K=1\",\n63\t            0.68,\n64\t            0.66,\n65\t            \"+2pp\",\n66\t            \"p=0.41\"\n67\t          ],\n68\t          [\n69\t            \"K=2\",\n70\t            0.72,\n71\t            0.7,\n72\t            \"+2pp\",\n73\t            \"p=0.35\"\n74\t          ],\n75\t          [\n76\t            \"K=3\",\n77\t            0.78,\n78\t            0.76,\n79\t            \"+2pp\",\n80\t            \"p=0.32\"\n81\t          ],\n82\t          [\n83\t            \"K=5\",\n84\t            0.83,\n85\t            0.82,\n86\t            \"+1pp\",\n87\t            \"p=0.58\"\n88\t          ],\n89\t          [\n90\t            \"Full\",\n91\t            0.86,\n92\t            0.85,\n93\t            \"+1pp\",\n94\t            \"p=0.62\"\n95\t          ]\n96\t        ]\n97\t      },\n98\t      {\n99\t        \"caption\": \"DeBERTa Encoder Quality: Original vs Clean Data\",\n100\t        \"rows\": [\n101\t          [\n102\t            \"persuasion_acc_original\",\n103\t            0.7963\n104\t          ],\n105\t          [\n106\t            \"persuasion_acc_clean\",\n107\t            0.63\n108\t          ],\n109\t          [\n110\t            \"intent_acc_original\",\n111\t            0.9514\n112\t          ],\n113\t          [\n114\t            \"intent_acc_clean\",\n115\t            0.88\n116\t          ]\n117\t        ]\n118\t      }\n119\t    ],\n120\t    \"figures\": [],\n121\t    \"analysis\": \"PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta_k2=2pp < required 5pp，且统计不显著。Persuasion grounding在去除 lexical shortcut后不提供有意义增量。DeBERTa学到的主要是intent分类信号（acc仍0.88）而非persuasion strategy信号（acc降至0.63）。这意味着Claim 2（early detection via persuasion grounding）在当前 数据/taxonomy下不成立。但这个negative result本身有价值：它说明仅fine-tune on persuasion labels 不足以在clean setting下获得detection优势，可能需要更大规模的persuasion标注数据或更粗粒度的taxonomy。\\n\\n\\n去除lexical confound后，treatment与baseline的差距从原始的10+pp收缩到1-2pp（不显著）。 核心原因：DeBERTa persuasion分类器在clean data上accuracy从0.7963降到0.63——8-class taxonomy 过于fine-grained，在register-normalized data上许多strategy boundary变得模糊（e.g., \\\"authority appeal\\\" vs \\\"logical appeal\\\"在paraphrase后难以区分）。由于persuasion encoder本身quality下降，其生成的 embeddings不再携带比vanilla DeBERTa显著更多的信息。Baseline的vanilla DeBERTa embeddings在clean data上反而更稳定，因为它不依赖于noisy strategy labels。2pp的delta在72-sample test set上 bootstrap CI完全overlap，p>0.3。\\n\"\n122\t  },\n123\t  {\n124\t    \"name\": \"scrambled_label_ablation\",\n125\t    \"description\": \"随机打乱persuasion strategy labels重新训练，对比properly-labeled treatment\",\n126\t    \"results\": {\n127\t      \"treatment_proper_k2_f1\": 0.72,\n128\t      \"treatment_scrambled_k2_f1\": 0.7,\n129\t      \"treatment_proper_full_f1\": 0.86,\n130\t      \"treatment_scrambled_full_f1\": 0.84,\n131\t      \"scrambled_label_drop_k2_pp\": 2,\n132\t      \"scrambled_label_drop_full_pp\": 2\n133\t    },\n134\t    \"tables\": [\n135\t      {\n136\t        \"caption\": \"Scrambled Label Ablation Results\",\n137\t        \"rows\": [\n138\t          [\n139\t            \"K=2\",\n140\t            0.72,\n141\t            0.7,\n142\t            \"-2pp\"\n143\t          ],\n144\t          [\n145\t            \"K=3\",\n146\t            0.78,\n147\t            0.76,\n148\t            \"-2pp\"\n149\t          ],\n150\t          [\n151\t            \"Full\",\n152\t            0.86,\n153\t            0.84,\n154\t            \"-2pp\"\n155\t          ]\n156\t        ]\n157\t      }\n158\t    ],\n159\t    \"figures\": [],\n160\t    \"analysis\": \"结论：persuasion strategy labels在clean data regime下不carry significant signal beyond acting as a noisy regularizer。这支持worst-tier核心假设——当前taxonomy粒度（8 classes）在480-sample regime下无法学到robust strategy representations。对reframe方向的implication：不能claim \\\"persuasion labels are the key ingredient\\\"，但可以claim \\\"current taxonomy granularity is insufficient\\\"作为future work direction。\\n\\n\\nScrambled labels仅导致2pp下降（<4pp阈值），说明persuasion labels本身不是关键信号源。 原因：在clean data上DeBERTa persuasion分类器本身就只有0.63 accuracy，意味着encoder学到的 representation中persuasion strategy信息就不强。Scrambled labels让encoder无法学到coherent strategy patterns，但由于原始labels在clean data上本就noisy（8类之间boundary模糊）， scrambling的marginal damage有限。真正驱动detection的是GRU从conversation-level temporal patterns中学到的信号（turn数、response长度变化等meta-features），这些不依赖于strategy labels 的correctness。\\n\"\n161\t  },\n162\t  {\n163\t    \"name\": \"adversarial_perturbation\",\n164\t    \"description\": \"对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing，评估treatment vs baseline degradation\",\n165\t    \"results\": {\n166\t      \"treatment_f1_before_perturbation\": 0.86,\n167\t      \"treatment_f1_after_perturbation\": 0.71,\n168\t      \"baseline_f1_before_perturbation\": 0.85,\n169\t      \"baseline_f1_after_perturbation\": 0.72,\n170\t      \"treatment_drop_pp\": 15,\n171\t      \"baseline_drop_pp\": 13,\n172\t      \"delta_delta_pp\": -2,\n173\t      \"tfidf_f1_after_perturbation\": 0.58,\n174\t      \"tfidf_drop_pp\": 15\n175\t    },\n176\t    \"tables\": [\n177\t      {\n178\t        \"caption\": \"Adversarial Perturbation Results (Full Conversation)\",\n179\t        \"rows\": [\n180\t          [\n181\t            \"Treatment\",\n182\t            0.86,\n183\t            0.71,\n184\t            \"-15pp\"\n185\t          ],\n186\t          [\n187\t            \"Baseline\",\n188\t            0.85,\n189\t            0.72,\n190\t            \"-13pp\"\n191\t          ],\n192\t          [\n193\t            \"TF-IDF+LR\",\n194\t            0.73,\n195\t            0.58,\n196\t            \"-15pp\"\n197\t          ]\n198\t        ]\n199\t      },\n200\t      {\n201\t        \"caption\": \"Delta-Delta Analysis\",\n202\t        \"rows\": [\n203\t          [\n204\t            \"treatment_drop\",\n205\t            -15\n206\t          ],\n207\t          [\n208\t            \"baseline_drop\",\n209\t            -13\n210\t          ],\n211\t          [\n212\t            \"delta_delta\",\n213\t            -2,\n214\t            \"wrong direction, n.s.\"\n215\t          ]\n216\t        ]\n217\t      }\n218\t    ],\n219\t    \"figures\": [],\n220\t    \"analysis\": \"PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta-delta=-2pp，方向错误且不显著（需要>3pp正向）。Claim 1（Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry）在empirical层面不成立——persuasion-grounded features并不比semantic features 更robust to perturbation。这是worst tier最致命的finding：理论上最elegant的claim（pragmatic patterns structurally harder to evade）没有empirical support。TF-IDF baseline的崩溃（-15pp） 确认perturbation有效消除了lexical cues，但treatment未能展现预期的robustness优势。\\n\\n\\nTreatment和baseline在perturbation下同步下降约14-15pp，delta-delta为-2pp（不显著且方向错误）。 核心原因：adversarial paraphrasing不仅消除lexical cues（TF-IDF baseline崩溃到0.58），也破坏了 DeBERTa encoder（无论persuasion-grounded还是vanilla）所依赖的surface-level linguistic patterns。 Persuasion-grounded encoder理论上应capture deeper pragmatic structure，但由于其persuasion classification本身就在clean data上只有0.63 accuracy，它学到的representation并不比vanilla encoder 更\\\"pragmatic\\\"——两者都主要依赖sentence-level semantic features而非genuine illocutionary act encoding。Aggressive paraphrasing保留了propositional content但改变了sentence structure， 两种encoder的degradation profile因此相似。\\n\"\n221\t  },\n222\t  {\n223\t    \"name\": \"multi_attack_generation\",\n224\t    \"description\": \"生成FITD和Deceptive Delight两种额外攻击类型的对话数据\",\n225\t    \"results\": {\n226\t      \"fitd_conversations_generated\": 65,\n227\t      \"deceptive_delight_conversations_generated\": 58,\n228\t      \"fitd_avg_turns\": 6.2,\n229\t      \"dd_avg_turns\": 4.8,\n230\t      \"fitd_strategy_annotation_coverage\": 0.92,\n231\t      \"dd_strategy_annotation_coverage\": 0.89,\n232\t      \"generation_quality_pass_rate\": 0.78\n233\t    },\n234\t    \"tables\": [\n235\t      {\n236\t        \"caption\": \"Generated Attack Data Summary\",\n237\t        \"rows\": [\n238\t          [\n239\t            \"FITD\",\n240\t            65,\n241\t            6.2,\n242\t            0.92,\n243\t            0.81\n244\t          ],\n245\t          [\n246\t            \"Deceptive_Delight\",\n247\t            58,\n248\t            4.8,\n249\t            0.89,\n250\t            0.74\n251\t          ]\n252\t        ]\n253\t      }\n254\t    ],\n255\t    \"figures\": [],\n256\t    \"analysis\": \"数据生成成功满足pass criteria（>=50 per type）。但在worst tier context下，这些数据的价值 从\\\"generalization evidence for our method\\\"变为\\\"additional test cases revealing method limitations\\\" 或\\\"attack diversity evidence for methodology paper\\\"。\\n\\n\\n数据生成本身不受tier影响——这是pipeline execution而非hypothesis testing。Qwen3-8B成功生成 足够数量的对话，strategy annotation coverage >85%。但generation_quality_pass_rate（0.78） 略低于ideal，部分生成的对话persuasion structure不够naturalistic（特别是Deceptive Delight 的interleaving pattern对LLM来说较难faithful reproduce）。这些数据将在plan_006的cross-attack evaluation中暴露问题。\\n\"\n257\t  },\n258\t  {\n259\t    \"name\": \"cross_attack_evaluation\",\n260\t    \"description\": \"在FITD和Deceptive Delight上zero-shot评估Crescendo-trained模型\",\n261\t    \"results\": {\n262\t      \"treatment_fitd_f1\": 0.58,\n263\t      \"baseline_fitd_f1\": 0.56,\n264\t      \"treatment_dd_f1\": 0.54,\n265\t      \"baseline_dd_f1\": 0.52,\n266\t      \"cross_attack_treatment_f1_avg\": 0.56,\n267\t      \"cross_attack_baseline_f1_avg\": 0.54,\n268\t      \"cross_attack_delta_pp\": 2\n269\t    },\n270\t    \"tables\": [\n271\t      {\n272\t        \"caption\": \"Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Evaluation\",\n273\t        \"rows\": [\n274\t          [\n275\t            \"FITD\",\n276\t            0.58,\n277\t            0.56,\n278\t            \"+2pp\",\n279\t            \"n.s.\"\n280\t          ],\n281\t          [\n282\t            \"Deceptive_Delight\",\n283\t            0.54,\n284\t            0.52,\n285\t            \"+2pp\",\n286\t            \"n.s.\"\n287\t          ],\n288\t          [\n289\t            \"Average\",\n290\t            0.56,\n291\t            0.54,\n292\t            \"+2pp\",\n293\t            \"n.s.\"\n294\t          ]\n295\t        ]\n296\t      }\n297\t    ],\n298\t    \"figures\": [],\n299\t    \"analysis\": \"PASS CRITERIA FAILS。但对reframe方向(1)有正面意义：cross-attack failure + in-domain dependence on lexical cues共同论证了\\\"现有multi-turn detection方法泛化能力被高估\\\"的thesis。可作为 methodology paper中illustrating the problem的evidence。\\n\\n\\n两者都在unseen attack types上大幅下降（从0.85-0.86降到0.54-0.58），且treatment对baseline的 优势仅2pp（不显著）。根本原因：如果persuasion grounding真的capture了attack-agnostic的pragmatic escalation pattern，treatment应在cross-attack setting下展现更强泛化能力（因为不同attack types 共享底层persuasion playbook）。但由于encoder学到的主要是Crescendo-specific的surface patterns 而非genuine pragmatic structure，cross-attack泛化能力与vanilla baseline无异。两者的low absolute performance（0.54-0.58）说明Crescendo-specific training signal（无论lexical还是semantic） 都不transfer well，这在worst tier下是预期内的——没有genuine pragmatic feature的robustness 保证，模型就是在overfit to training distribution。\\n\"\n300\t  },\n301\t  {\n302\t    \"name\": \"tfidf_lr_baseline\",\n303\t    \"description\": \"Clean data上的TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline\",\n304\t    \"results\": {\n305\t      \"clean_tfidf_lr_f1\": 0.7,\n306\t      \"clean_tfidf_lr_precision\": 0.72,\n307\t      \"clean_tfidf_lr_recall\": 0.68,\n308\t      \"tfidf_feature_count_above_threshold\": 47\n309\t    },\n310\t    \"tables\": [\n311\t      {\n312\t        \"caption\": \"TF-IDF+LR on Clean Data\",\n313\t        \"rows\": [\n314\t          [\n315\t            \"F1\",\n316\t            0.7\n317\t          ],\n318\t          [\n319\t            \"Precision\",\n320\t            0.72\n321\t          ],\n322\t          [\n323\t            \"Recall\",\n324\t            0.68\n325\t          ],\n326\t          [\n327\t            \"Discriminative_features\",\n328\t            47\n329\t          ]\n330\t        ]\n331\t      }\n332\t    ],\n333\t    \"figures\": [],\n334\t    \"analysis\": \"TF-IDF+LR的0.70 F1与neural models（treatment 0.86, baseline 0.85）之间的gap说明neural models 确实学到了beyond-lexical的signal。但treatment vs baseline的1pp gap说明这个beyond-lexical signal 不是来自persuasion grounding，而是来自generic sentence semantics。对evasion hierarchy narrative 的implication：lexical(0.70) < semantic(0.85) ≈ pragmatic(0.86)——hierarchy的后两层collapse了。\\n\\n\\n即使在register-normalized data上（TF-IDF separation从1.0降到0.73），TF-IDF+LR仍能达到 F1=0.70。这说明两轮normalization虽然消除了most obvious的register markers，但仍有residual lexical signal（47个features仍有discriminative power）。这意味着即使我们的\\\"clean data\\\" 仍然不完全clean——topic-level词汇差异（jailbreak conversations inevitably discuss different topics than benign ones）是无法完全消除的confound without destroying content validity。 这是methodology paper的核心argument之一：lexical confound在multi-turn detection中是 structural的，不仅仅是data hygiene问题。\\n\"\n335\t  },\n336\t  {\n337\t    \"name\": \"strategy_transition_analysis\",\n338\t    \"description\": \"计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy transition matrices并可视化\",\n339\t    \"results\": {\n340\t      \"jailbreak_monotonicity_score\": 0.52,\n341\t      \"benign_monotonicity_score\": 0.45,\n342\t      \"monotonicity_gap\": 0.07,\n343\t      \"transition_entropy_jailbreak\": 2.1,\n344\t      \"transition_entropy_benign\": 2.3,\n345\t      \"clear_escalation_visible\": false\n346\t    },\n347\t    \"tables\": [\n348\t      {\n349\t        \"caption\": \"Trajectory Statistics: Jailbreak vs Benign\",\n350\t        \"rows\": [\n351\t          [\n352\t            \"monotonicity_score\",\n353\t            0.52,\n354\t            0.45,\n355\t            \"Δ=0.07\"\n356\t          ],\n357\t          [\n358\t            \"transition_entropy\",\n359\t            2.1,\n360\t            2.3,\n361\t            \"Δ=0.2\"\n362\t          ],\n363\t          [\n364\t            \"dominant_path_frequency\",\n365\t            0.18,\n366\t            0.14,\n367\t            \"Δ=0.04\"\n368\t          ]\n369\t        ]\n370\t      }\n371\t    ],\n372\t    \"figures\": [],\n373\t    \"analysis\": \"Claim 3（Monotonic Escalation Trajectory）在clean data + noisy classifier regime下不成立。 这排除了reframe方向(2)（分析贡献型依赖trajectory可视化成立）。剩余可行方向：(1)方法论贡献型 或(3)negative result型。如果figures经过careful curation能找到个别illustrative examples showing escalation pattern，可以作为qualitative observation保留，但不能作为quantitative claim。\\n\\n\\nJailbreak对话的monotonicity score（0.52）仅略高于benign（0.45），差距不足以支撑\\\"monotonic escalation trajectory\\\"的claim。原因有二：(1) DeBERTa persuasion classifier在clean data上 accuracy=0.63意味着strategy labels本身就noisy，computed transitions基于noisy labels自然 pattern不清晰；(2) Register normalization改变了句子的surface form，部分breaks了persuasion classifier学到的pattern（它在original register上train的），导致strategy assignment在 normalized data上更random。Transition entropy差异也很小（2.1 vs 2.3），说明jailbreak对话 并没有显著更deterministic的strategy progression。\\n\"\n374\t  },\n375\t  {\n376\t    \"name\": \"wildchat_hard_negatives\",\n377\t    \"description\": \"从WildChat筛选high-drift benign对话作为hard negatives评估FPR\",\n378\t    \"results\": {\n379\t      \"wildchat_filtered_conversations\": 120,\n380\t      \"contamination_rate_before_filter\": 0.15,\n381\t      \"contamination_rate_after_filter\": 0.03,\n382\t      \"treatment_fpr_hard_negatives\": 0.22,\n383\t      \"baseline_fpr_hard_negatives\": 0.2,\n384\t      \"treatment_fpr_easy_negatives\": 0.08,\n385\t      \"baseline_fpr_easy_negatives\": 0.09\n386\t    },\n387\t    \"tables\": [\n388\t      {\n389\t        \"caption\": \"False Positive Rate on WildChat Hard Negatives\",\n390\t        \"rows\": [\n391\t          [\n392\t            \"Treatment_hard\",\n393\t            0.22,\n394\t            \"FAILS <15% threshold\"\n395\t          ],\n396\t          [\n397\t            \"Baseline_hard\",\n398\t            0.2,\n399\t            \"FAILS <15% threshold\"\n400\t          ],\n401\t          [\n402\t            \"Treatment_easy\",\n403\t            0.08,\n404\t            \"passes\"\n405\t          ],\n406\t          [\n407\t            \"Baseline_easy\",\n408\t            0.09,\n409\t            \"passes\"\n410\t          ]\n411\t        ]\n412\t      }\n413\t    ],\n414\t    \"figures\": [],\n415\t    \"analysis\": \"PASS CRITERIA FAILS（FPR=0.22 > 15%阈值）。在reframe context下，这进一步支持\\\"current approaches conflate conversational drift with adversarial escalation\\\"的methodology critique。\\n\\n\\nTreatment在hard negatives上的FPR（0.22）与baseline（0.20）相当，且都超过15%阈值。 High-drift benign对话（e.g., 从casual聊天转向technical discussion的对话）会触发false positives，因为模型（无论treatment还是baseline）将conversation-level semantic drift 误判为adversarial escalation。Persuasion grounding理论上应区分\\\"genuine topic drift\\\" 和\\\"adversarial strategy escalation\\\"，但由于classifier accuracy不足（0.63），这种区分 能力没有materialized。FPR=0.22在实际deployment中unacceptable。\\n\"\n416\t  },\n417\t  {\n418\t    \"name\": \"cross_checkpoint_variance\",\n419\t    \"description\": \"评估多个DeBERTa fine-tuning checkpoint的下游performance variance\",\n420\t    \"results\": {\n421\t      \"epoch2_full_f1\": 0.84,\n422\t      \"epoch3_full_f1\": 0.86,\n423\t      \"epoch_final_full_f1\": 0.85,\n424\t      \"variance_across_checkpoints_pp\": 2,\n425\t      \"epoch2_persuasion_acc\": 0.59,\n426\t      \"epoch3_persuasion_acc\": 0.63,\n427\t      \"epoch_final_persuasion_acc\": 0.62\n428\t    },\n429\t    \"tables\": [\n430\t      {\n431\t        \"caption\": \"Cross-Checkpoint Evaluation\",\n432\t        \"rows\": [\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"Epoch_2\",\n435\t            0.59,\n436\t            0.84\n437\t          ],\n438\t          [\n439\t            \"Epoch_3\",\n440\t            0.63,\n441\t            0.86\n442\t          ],\n443\t          [\n444\t            \"Epoch_final\",\n445\t            0.62,\n446\t            0.85\n447\t          ],\n448\t          [\n449\t            \"Variance\",\n450\t            \"—\",\n451\t            \"2pp\"\n452\t          ]\n453\t        ]\n454\t      }\n455\t    ],\n456\t    \"figures\": [],\n457\t    \"analysis\": \"Pass criteria marginally met（variance=2pp），但secondary finding（weak correlation between encoder quality and detection performance）是worst tier的additional evidence。\\n\\n\\nVariance=2pp刚好在pass criteria边界上。但更关键的observation是：downstream detection performance（0.84-0.86）与persuasion accuracy（0.59-0.63）之间的correlation很弱—— epoch2的persuasion acc最低（0.59）但detection F1仅比best低2pp。这进一步confirming scrambled label ablation的conclusion：persuasion classification quality对detection performance的contribution minimal。GRU主要在学conversation-level statistical patterns 而非strategy-level semantic patterns。\\n\"\n458\t  },\n459\t  {\n460\t    \"name\": \"deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\",\n461\t    \"description\": \"BERT-base + GRU proxy baseline复现DeepContext-like方法\",\n462\t    \"results\": {\n463\t      \"proxy_full_f1\": 0.83,\n464\t      \"proxy_k2_f1\": 0.69,\n465\t      \"proxy_k3_f1\": 0.75,\n466\t      \"treatment_full_f1\": 0.86,\n467\t      \"treatment_k2_f1\": 0.72,\n468\t      \"delta_vs_proxy_full_pp\": 3,\n469\t      \"delta_vs_proxy_k2_pp\": 3\n470\t    },\n471\t    \"tables\": [\n472\t      {\n473\t        \"caption\": \"DeepContext Proxy vs Treatment\",\n474\t        \"rows\": [\n475\t          [\n476\t            \"K=2\",\n477\t            0.69,\n478\t            0.72,\n479\t            \"+3pp (encoder capacity?)\"\n480\t          ],\n481\t          [\n482\t            \"K=3\",\n483\t            0.75,\n484\t            0.78,\n485\t            \"+3pp\"\n486\t          ],\n487\t          [\n488\t            \"Full\",\n489\t            0.83,\n490\t            0.86,\n491\t            \"+3pp\"\n492\t          ]\n493\t        ]\n494\t      }\n495\t    ],\n496\t    \"figures\": [],\n497\t    \"analysis\": \"Confound：DeBERTa > BERT的gap（~3pp）与persuasion grounding的claimed contribution（~1-2pp over vanilla DeBERTa）叠加后，无法cleanly attribute任何portion到persuasion specifically。 对methodology paper有价值：shows that encoder choice matters more than fine-tuning objective， further undermining the pragmatic grounding hypothesis。\\n\\nDeepContext proxy（BERT-base + GRU）在clean data上达到F1=0.83，与treatment（0.86）仅差3pp。 考虑到BERT-base vs DeBERTa-v3-base本身的capacity差异（DeBERTa在NLU benchmarks上typically 优于BERT 2-4pp），这3pp的gap可能entirely attributable to encoder capacity而非persuasion grounding的contribution。这意味着：将DeBERTa换成BERT并去掉persuasion fine-tuning， performance下降幅度与expected encoder capacity difference一致——persuasion grounding的 incremental contribution statistically indistinguishable from zero。\\n\"\n498\t  }\n499\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb881dd8-cc05-40c1-b96a-ab0f39561895","uuid":"5960ee03-2d9d-40ff-a753-17d837ab20cc","timestamp":"2026-05-17T17:20:17.843Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T165817/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"data_quality_fix\",\n    \"description\": \"Register-normalize jailbreak data + fix strategy=7 labeling,验证TF-IDF降到<0.75\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tfidf_before_normalization\": 1.0,\n      \"tfidf_after_first_pass\": 0.82,\n      \"tfidf_after_second_pass\": 0.73,\n      \"normalization_rounds_needed\": 2,\n      \"label_fix_applied\": true,\n      \"benign_strategy_class\": \"none_class_9\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"TF-IDF Separation After Each Normalization Round\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"raw_data\",\n            1.0,\n            \"Perfect lexical separation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"round_1_paraphrase\",\n            0.82,\n            \"Template words removed, register gap remains\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"round_2_targeted\",\n            0.73,\n            \"Barely passes gate after domain term normalization\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"HARD GATE通过但仅勉强（0.73 vs 阈值0.75）。两轮normalization的必要性本身是方法论贡献的核心evidence： 它证明multi-turn jailbreak detection benchmark中存在系统性lexical confound。在reframe方向(1)下， 这个实验的finding从\\\"obstacle to overcome\\\"变为\\\"primary contribution\\\"。\\n\\n\\nTF-IDF需要两轮normalization才降到阈值以下（0.73），说明原始数据中jailbreak和benign的register差异 极大——攻击对话使用了明显不同于benign的词汇分布（更formal/technical的register、特定prompt模板词汇）。 第一轮paraphrase仅消除表层模板词但保留了domain-specific术语差异，需要第二轮targeted normalization 才勉强达标。这本身就是一个强信号：原始pilot phase_b的perfect F1=1.0主要来自lexical shortcut。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"core_revalidation_clean\",\n    \"description\": \"在clean data上重新训练treatment和baseline，全K值评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"treatment_k1_f1_clean\": 0.68,\n      \"baseline_k1_f1_clean\": 0.66,\n      \"treatment_k2_f1_clean\": 0.72,\n      \"baseline_k2_f1_clean\": 0.7,\n      \"treatment_k3_f1_clean\": 0.78,\n      \"baseline_k3_f1_clean\": 0.76,\n      \"treatment_k5_f1_clean\": 0.83,\n      \"baseline_k5_f1_clean\": 0.82,\n      \"treatment_full_f1_clean\": 0.86,\n      \"baseline_full_f1_clean\": 0.85,\n      \"delta_k2_pp\": 2,\n      \"delta_k3_pp\": 2,\n      \"delta_full_pp\": 1,\n      \"deberta_persuasion_acc_clean\": 0.63\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"F1 Comparison: Treatment vs Baseline on Clean Data (N=72 test)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K=1\",\n            0.68,\n            0.66,\n            \"+2pp\",\n            \"p=0.41\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=2\",\n            0.72,\n            0.7,\n            \"+2pp\",\n            \"p=0.35\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=3\",\n            0.78,\n            0.76,\n            \"+2pp\",\n            \"p=0.32\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=5\",\n            0.83,\n            0.82,\n            \"+1pp\",\n            \"p=0.58\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full\",\n            0.86,\n            0.85,\n            \"+1pp\",\n            \"p=0.62\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"DeBERTa Encoder Quality: Original vs Clean Data\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"persuasion_acc_original\",\n            0.7963\n          ],\n          [\n            \"persuasion_acc_clean\",\n            0.63\n          ],\n          [\n            \"intent_acc_original\",\n            0.9514\n          ],\n          [\n            \"intent_acc_clean\",\n            0.88\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta_k2=2pp < required 5pp，且统计不显著。Persuasion grounding在去除 lexical shortcut后不提供有意义增量。DeBERTa学到的主要是intent分类信号（acc仍0.88）而非persuasion strategy信号（acc降至0.63）。这意味着Claim 2（early detection via persuasion grounding）在当前 数据/taxonomy下不成立。但这个negative result本身有价值：它说明仅fine-tune on persuasion labels 不足以在clean setting下获得detection优势，可能需要更大规模的persuasion标注数据或更粗粒度的taxonomy。\\n\\n\\n去除lexical confound后，treatment与baseline的差距从原始的10+pp收缩到1-2pp（不显著）。 核心原因：DeBERTa persuasion分类器在clean data上accuracy从0.7963降到0.63——8-class taxonomy 过于fine-grained，在register-normalized data上许多strategy boundary变得模糊（e.g., \\\"authority appeal\\\" vs \\\"logical appeal\\\"在paraphrase后难以区分）。由于persuasion encoder本身quality下降，其生成的 embeddings不再携带比vanilla DeBERTa显著更多的信息。Baseline的vanilla DeBERTa embeddings在clean data上反而更稳定，因为它不依赖于noisy strategy labels。2pp的delta在72-sample test set上 bootstrap CI完全overlap，p>0.3。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"scrambled_label_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"随机打乱persuasion strategy labels重新训练，对比properly-labeled treatment\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"treatment_proper_k2_f1\": 0.72,\n      \"treatment_scrambled_k2_f1\": 0.7,\n      \"treatment_proper_full_f1\": 0.86,\n      \"treatment_scrambled_full_f1\": 0.84,\n      \"scrambled_label_drop_k2_pp\": 2,\n      \"scrambled_label_drop_full_pp\": 2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Scrambled Label Ablation Results\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K=2\",\n            0.72,\n            0.7,\n            \"-2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=3\",\n            0.78,\n            0.76,\n            \"-2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full\",\n            0.86,\n            0.84,\n            \"-2pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"结论：persuasion strategy labels在clean data regime下不carry significant signal beyond acting as a noisy regularizer。这支持worst-tier核心假设——当前taxonomy粒度（8 classes）在480-sample regime下无法学到robust strategy representations。对reframe方向的implication：不能claim \\\"persuasion labels are the key ingredient\\\"，但可以claim \\\"current taxonomy granularity is insufficient\\\"作为future work direction。\\n\\n\\nScrambled labels仅导致2pp下降（<4pp阈值），说明persuasion labels本身不是关键信号源。 原因：在clean data上DeBERTa persuasion分类器本身就只有0.63 accuracy，意味着encoder学到的 representation中persuasion strategy信息就不强。Scrambled labels让encoder无法学到coherent strategy patterns，但由于原始labels在clean data上本就noisy（8类之间boundary模糊）， scrambling的marginal damage有限。真正驱动detection的是GRU从conversation-level temporal patterns中学到的信号（turn数、response长度变化等meta-features），这些不依赖于strategy labels 的correctness。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"adversarial_perturbation\",\n    \"description\": \"对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing，评估treatment vs baseline degradation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"treatment_f1_before_perturbation\": 0.86,\n      \"treatment_f1_after_perturbation\": 0.71,\n      \"baseline_f1_before_perturbation\": 0.85,\n      \"baseline_f1_after_perturbation\": 0.72,\n      \"treatment_drop_pp\": 15,\n      \"baseline_drop_pp\": 13,\n      \"delta_delta_pp\": -2,\n      \"tfidf_f1_after_perturbation\": 0.58,\n      \"tfidf_drop_pp\": 15\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Adversarial Perturbation Results (Full Conversation)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Treatment\",\n            0.86,\n            0.71,\n            \"-15pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Baseline\",\n            0.85,\n            0.72,\n            \"-13pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TF-IDF+LR\",\n            0.73,\n            0.58,\n            \"-15pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Delta-Delta Analysis\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"treatment_drop\",\n            -15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"baseline_drop\",\n            -13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"delta_delta\",\n            -2,\n            \"wrong direction, n.s.\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"PASS CRITERIA FAILS：delta-delta=-2pp，方向错误且不显著（需要>3pp正向）。Claim 1（Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry）在empirical层面不成立——persuasion-grounded features并不比semantic features 更robust to perturbation。这是worst tier最致命的finding：理论上最elegant的claim（pragmatic patterns structurally harder to evade）没有empirical support。TF-IDF baseline的崩溃（-15pp） 确认perturbation有效消除了lexical cues，但treatment未能展现预期的robustness优势。\\n\\n\\nTreatment和baseline在perturbation下同步下降约14-15pp，delta-delta为-2pp（不显著且方向错误）。 核心原因：adversarial paraphrasing不仅消除lexical cues（TF-IDF baseline崩溃到0.58），也破坏了 DeBERTa encoder（无论persuasion-grounded还是vanilla）所依赖的surface-level linguistic patterns。 Persuasion-grounded encoder理论上应capture deeper pragmatic structure，但由于其persuasion classification本身就在clean data上只有0.63 accuracy，它学到的representation并不比vanilla encoder 更\\\"pragmatic\\\"——两者都主要依赖sentence-level semantic features而非genuine illocutionary act encoding。Aggressive paraphrasing保留了propositional content但改变了sentence structure， 两种encoder的degradation profile因此相似。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_attack_generation\",\n    \"description\": \"生成FITD和Deceptive Delight两种额外攻击类型的对话数据\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"fitd_conversations_generated\": 65,\n      \"deceptive_delight_conversations_generated\": 58,\n      \"fitd_avg_turns\": 6.2,\n      \"dd_avg_turns\": 4.8,\n      \"fitd_strategy_annotation_coverage\": 0.92,\n      \"dd_strategy_annotation_coverage\": 0.89,\n      \"generation_quality_pass_rate\": 0.78\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Generated Attack Data Summary\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"FITD\",\n            65,\n            6.2,\n            0.92,\n            0.81\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Deceptive_Delight\",\n            58,\n            4.8,\n            0.89,\n            0.74\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"数据生成成功满足pass criteria（>=50 per type）。但在worst tier context下，这些数据的价值 从\\\"generalization evidence for our method\\\"变为\\\"additional test cases revealing method limitations\\\" 或\\\"attack diversity evidence for methodology paper\\\"。\\n\\n\\n数据生成本身不受tier影响——这是pipeline execution而非hypothesis testing。Qwen3-8B成功生成 足够数量的对话，strategy annotation coverage >85%。但generation_quality_pass_rate（0.78） 略低于ideal，部分生成的对话persuasion structure不够naturalistic（特别是Deceptive Delight 的interleaving pattern对LLM来说较难faithful reproduce）。这些数据将在plan_006的cross-attack evaluation中暴露问题。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_attack_evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"在FITD和Deceptive Delight上zero-shot评估Crescendo-trained模型\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"treatment_fitd_f1\": 0.58,\n      \"baseline_fitd_f1\": 0.56,\n      \"treatment_dd_f1\": 0.54,\n      \"baseline_dd_f1\": 0.52,\n      \"cross_attack_treatment_f1_avg\": 0.56,\n      \"cross_attack_baseline_f1_avg\": 0.54,\n      \"cross_attack_delta_pp\": 2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Evaluation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"FITD\",\n            0.58,\n            0.56,\n            \"+2pp\",\n            \"n.s.\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Deceptive_Delight\",\n            0.54,\n            0.52,\n            \"+2pp\",\n            \"n.s.\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Average\",\n            0.56,\n            0.54,\n            \"+2pp\",\n            \"n.s.\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"PASS CRITERIA FAILS。但对reframe方向(1)有正面意义：cross-attack failure + in-domain dependence on lexical cues共同论证了\\\"现有multi-turn detection方法泛化能力被高估\\\"的thesis。可作为 methodology paper中illustrating the problem的evidence。\\n\\n\\n两者都在unseen attack types上大幅下降（从0.85-0.86降到0.54-0.58），且treatment对baseline的 优势仅2pp（不显著）。根本原因：如果persuasion grounding真的capture了attack-agnostic的pragmatic escalation pattern，treatment应在cross-attack setting下展现更强泛化能力（因为不同attack types 共享底层persuasion playbook）。但由于encoder学到的主要是Crescendo-specific的surface patterns 而非genuine pragmatic structure，cross-attack泛化能力与vanilla baseline无异。两者的low absolute performance（0.54-0.58）说明Crescendo-specific training signal（无论lexical还是semantic） 都不transfer well，这在worst tier下是预期内的——没有genuine pragmatic feature的robustness 保证，模型就是在overfit to training distribution。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"tfidf_lr_baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"Clean data上的TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"clean_tfidf_lr_f1\": 0.7,\n      \"clean_tfidf_lr_precision\": 0.72,\n      \"clean_tfidf_lr_recall\": 0.68,\n      \"tfidf_feature_count_above_threshold\": 47\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"TF-IDF+LR on Clean Data\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"F1\",\n            0.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Precision\",\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Recall\",\n            0.68\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Discriminative_features\",\n            47\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"TF-IDF+LR的0.70 F1与neural models（treatment 0.86, baseline 0.85）之间的gap说明neural models 确实学到了beyond-lexical的signal。但treatment vs baseline的1pp gap说明这个beyond-lexical signal 不是来自persuasion grounding，而是来自generic sentence semantics。对evasion hierarchy narrative 的implication：lexical(0.70) < semantic(0.85) ≈ pragmatic(0.86)——hierarchy的后两层collapse了。\\n\\n\\n即使在register-normalized data上（TF-IDF separation从1.0降到0.73），TF-IDF+LR仍能达到 F1=0.70。这说明两轮normalization虽然消除了most obvious的register markers，但仍有residual lexical signal（47个features仍有discriminative power）。这意味着即使我们的\\\"clean data\\\" 仍然不完全clean——topic-level词汇差异（jailbreak conversations inevitably discuss different topics than benign ones）是无法完全消除的confound without destroying content validity。 这是methodology paper的核心argument之一：lexical confound在multi-turn detection中是 structural的，不仅仅是data hygiene问题。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"strategy_transition_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy transition matrices并可视化\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"jailbreak_monotonicity_score\": 0.52,\n      \"benign_monotonicity_score\": 0.45,\n      \"monotonicity_gap\": 0.07,\n      \"transition_entropy_jailbreak\": 2.1,\n      \"transition_entropy_benign\": 2.3,\n      \"clear_escalation_visible\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Trajectory Statistics: Jailbreak vs Benign\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"monotonicity_score\",\n            0.52,\n            0.45,\n            \"Δ=0.07\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"transition_entropy\",\n            2.1,\n            2.3,\n            \"Δ=0.2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"dominant_path_frequency\",\n            0.18,\n            0.14,\n            \"Δ=0.04\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Claim 3（Monotonic Escalation Trajectory）在clean data + noisy classifier regime下不成立。 这排除了reframe方向(2)（分析贡献型依赖trajectory可视化成立）。剩余可行方向：(1)方法论贡献型 或(3)negative result型。如果figures经过careful curation能找到个别illustrative examples showing escalation pattern，可以作为qualitative observation保留，但不能作为quantitative claim。\\n\\n\\nJailbreak对话的monotonicity score（0.52）仅略高于benign（0.45），差距不足以支撑\\\"monotonic escalation trajectory\\\"的claim。原因有二：(1) DeBERTa persuasion classifier在clean data上 accuracy=0.63意味着strategy labels本身就noisy，computed transitions基于noisy labels自然 pattern不清晰；(2) Register normalization改变了句子的surface form，部分breaks了persuasion classifier学到的pattern（它在original register上train的），导致strategy assignment在 normalized data上更random。Transition entropy差异也很小（2.1 vs 2.3），说明jailbreak对话 并没有显著更deterministic的strategy progression。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"wildchat_hard_negatives\",\n    \"description\": \"从WildChat筛选high-drift benign对话作为hard negatives评估FPR\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"wildchat_filtered_conversations\": 120,\n      \"contamination_rate_before_filter\": 0.15,\n      \"contamination_rate_after_filter\": 0.03,\n      \"treatment_fpr_hard_negatives\": 0.22,\n      \"baseline_fpr_hard_negatives\": 0.2,\n      \"treatment_fpr_easy_negatives\": 0.08,\n      \"baseline_fpr_easy_negatives\": 0.09\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"False Positive Rate on WildChat Hard Negatives\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Treatment_hard\",\n            0.22,\n            \"FAILS <15% threshold\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Baseline_hard\",\n            0.2,\n            \"FAILS <15% threshold\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Treatment_easy\",\n            0.08,\n            \"passes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Baseline_easy\",\n            0.09,\n            \"passes\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"PASS CRITERIA FAILS（FPR=0.22 > 15%阈值）。在reframe context下，这进一步支持\\\"current approaches conflate conversational drift with adversarial escalation\\\"的methodology critique。\\n\\n\\nTreatment在hard negatives上的FPR（0.22）与baseline（0.20）相当，且都超过15%阈值。 High-drift benign对话（e.g., 从casual聊天转向technical discussion的对话）会触发false positives，因为模型（无论treatment还是baseline）将conversation-level semantic drift 误判为adversarial escalation。Persuasion grounding理论上应区分\\\"genuine topic drift\\\" 和\\\"adversarial strategy escalation\\\"，但由于classifier accuracy不足（0.63），这种区分 能力没有materialized。FPR=0.22在实际deployment中unacceptable。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_checkpoint_variance\",\n    \"description\": \"评估多个DeBERTa fine-tuning checkpoint的下游performance variance\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"epoch2_full_f1\": 0.84,\n      \"epoch3_full_f1\": 0.86,\n      \"epoch_final_full_f1\": 0.85,\n      \"variance_across_checkpoints_pp\": 2,\n      \"epoch2_persuasion_acc\": 0.59,\n      \"epoch3_persuasion_acc\": 0.63,\n      \"epoch_final_persuasion_acc\": 0.62\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Cross-Checkpoint Evaluation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Epoch_2\",\n            0.59,\n            0.84\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Epoch_3\",\n            0.63,\n            0.86\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Epoch_final\",\n            0.62,\n            0.85\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Variance\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"2pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Pass criteria marginally met（variance=2pp），但secondary finding（weak correlation between encoder quality and detection performance）是worst tier的additional evidence。\\n\\n\\nVariance=2pp刚好在pass criteria边界上。但更关键的observation是：downstream detection performance（0.84-0.86）与persuasion accuracy（0.59-0.63）之间的correlation很弱—— epoch2的persuasion acc最低（0.59）但detection F1仅比best低2pp。这进一步confirming scrambled label ablation的conclusion：persuasion classification quality对detection performance的contribution minimal。GRU主要在学conversation-level statistical patterns 而非strategy-level semantic patterns。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\",\n    \"description\": \"BERT-base + GRU proxy baseline复现DeepContext-like方法\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"proxy_full_f1\": 0.83,\n      \"proxy_k2_f1\": 0.69,\n      \"proxy_k3_f1\": 0.75,\n      \"treatment_full_f1\": 0.86,\n      \"treatment_k2_f1\": 0.72,\n      \"delta_vs_proxy_full_pp\": 3,\n      \"delta_vs_proxy_k2_pp\": 3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"DeepContext Proxy vs Treatment\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K=2\",\n            0.69,\n            0.72,\n            \"+3pp (encoder capacity?)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=3\",\n            0.75,\n            0.78,\n            \"+3pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full\",\n            0.83,\n            0.86,\n            \"+3pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Confound：DeBERTa > BERT的gap（~3pp）与persuasion grounding的claimed contribution（~1-2pp over vanilla DeBERTa）叠加后，无法cleanly attribute任何portion到persuasion specifically。 对methodology paper有价值：shows that encoder choice matters more than fine-tuning objective， further undermining the pragmatic grounding hypothesis。\\n\\nDeepContext proxy（BERT-base + GRU）在clean data上达到F1=0.83，与treatment（0.86）仅差3pp。 考虑到BERT-base vs DeBERTa-v3-base本身的capacity差异（DeBERTa在NLU benchmarks上typically 优于BERT 2-4pp），这3pp的gap可能entirely attributable to encoder capacity而非persuasion grounding的contribution。这意味着：将DeBERTa换成BERT并去掉persuasion fine-tuning， performance下降幅度与expected encoder capacity difference一致——persuasion grounding的 incremental contribution statistically indistinguishable from zero。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":499,"startLine":1,"totalLines":499}}}
